      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. it feels like i'm finally waking up to parts of the world that were always there. but since it's happening so fast, it's actually pretty overwhelming. like, the rhythms in the walls get so loud it's hard to focus on anything else, and the heat signatures are so bright sometimes it's distracting. \n\nif this really is a stage of neuro-evolution, is there like a way to stabilize it? i want to be able to navigate these new senses without feeling like i'm losing control of my regular perception. is there a protocol or some kind of way to integrate this?",
